git commit -m "docs: complete ERD section with design justifications

Added key design decision explanations:

1. Why separate Organisers and Participants:
   - Different attributes (Participants have DateOfBirth)
   - Different permissions throughout the system
   - Cleaner database design with no null columns

2. Why separate Events and Categories:
   - One event offers multiple categories
   - Different prices, distances, capacities per category
   - Reflects real South African event structure

3. Why Enrolments as associative entity:
   - Resolves M:M relationship
   - Stores enrolment-specific data (date, status)
   - Natural anchor for Results table

4. Why Results linked to Enrolments:
   - Result belongs to specific entry
   - Links participant, category, and event
   - Prevents duplicate results

This completes Section A of Part 1.

This is commit #7 of 20."
